---
import { Image, getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import headshot from '../assets/david-salazar-headshot.jpg';
import calendar from '../assets/tetsu-calendar.png';
import progress from '../assets/tetsu-progress.png';
import aiImport from '../assets/tetsu-ai-import.png';
import logo from '../assets/tetsu-logo.jpg';
import hackathon from '../assets/computershare-hackathon.jpg';

const big = async (src) => (await getImage({ src, width: 1000, format: 'webp' })).src;
const full = {
  calendar: await big(calendar),
  progress: await big(progress),
  aiImport: await big(aiImport),
};
---

<Base
  title="David Salazar · Business analysis and project delivery"
  description="David Salazar writes clear requirements from messy problems and builds working prototypes, with AI in the workflow and a human reviewing the result."
  current="intro"
>
  
    <section class="hero" id="intro">
<div class="col hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <h1 data-reveal>Clear requirements from messy problems.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lead" data-reveal>
          I do business analysis and project coordination, currently as a consultant at FDM
          Group. I write requirements and acceptance criteria, and I build prototypes with AI and
          check them against those requirements and tests.
        </p>
        <div class="actions" data-reveal>
          <a class="btn" href="/work/tetsu/">Read the Tetsu case study</a>
          <a class="btn soft" href="/David_Salazar_Resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Resume (PDF)</a>
          <a class="textlink" href="mailto:davesal0710@gmail.com">Email me</a>
        </div>
        <div class="who" data-reveal>
          <Image src={headshot} alt="" width={56} height={56} densities={[1, 2]} loading="eager" />
          <p>
            <strong>David Salazar</strong>
            New York · open to business analyst, implementation and automation roles
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a class="hero-phone" href="/work/tetsu/" data-reveal>
        <img src="/tetsu-import.gif" data-poster="/tetsu-import-poster.png" width="320" height="696" alt="Tetsu’s import screen: a pasted routine is organized, then shown on a review screen before anything is replaced" />
        <span>Tetsu, my workout app. Paste a routine, review it, then save.</span>
      </a>
</div>

<div class="col hero-demo">
      <div class="demo" data-ui data-reveal>
        <p class="label muted small" style="margin:0 0 0.75rem">How I write a requirement, using Tetsu. Written for this page from the case study.</p>
        <div data-demo>
          <div data-pane data-label="Note">
            <span class="label">What a user might say (a working persona, not an interview)</span>
            <p>
              “My whole routine lives in my notes app: bench 135&nbsp;lb for 8, dumbbell curls 27.5&nbsp;lb
              for 12. Every tracker makes me retype it, and I’m afraid I’ll lose my numbers.”
            </p>
          </div>
          <div data-pane data-label="User story">
            <span class="label">What the product has to do for them</span>
            <p>
              As a lifter who keeps my routine in a notes app, I want to paste it in and check how
              it was read before anything is saved, so that I keep my numbers exactly as written.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div data-pane data-label="Criteria">
            <span class="label">How we know it works</span>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Given pasted text with decimal weights like 27.5&nbsp;lb, when it is imported, then
                every value is kept exactly as written.
              </li>
              <li>
                Given an import, when the review screen shows, then nothing replaces the current
                plan until I confirm.
              </li>
              <li>
                Given a backup restore, when a day already has data, then that day is not
                overwritten.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
</div>
    </section>

    <section id="work">
<div class="col">
      <h2 data-reveal>work</h2>

      <article class="piece side">
        <h3 data-reveal>Tetsu, a workout planner and training log</h3>
        <p class="meta" data-reveal>Solo project, live as an installable web app</p>
        <p data-reveal>
          People who lift seriously keep their routines in notes and spreadsheets, and most trackers
          make them retype everything into rigid templates. I defined the problem, three working
          personas and the requirements: paste a routine in and review it before it replaces
          anything, log sets without a signal, and get progression advice that says “hold” when the
          history doesn’t support adding weight.
        </p>
        <p data-reveal>
          I owned the product. AI coding assistants (Codex and Claude Code) wrote the code under my
          direction, with a pull request for every change.
        </p>
        <div class="shots" data-reveal>
          <figure>
            <Image
              src={calendar} data-full={full.calendar}
              alt="Tetsu’s month calendar on a phone, with push, pull and legs days marked"
              widths={[160, 320]}
              sizes="(min-width: 40rem) 11rem, 30vw"
            />
            <figcaption>Calendar</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <Image
              src={progress} data-full={full.progress}
              alt="Tetsu’s progress tab on a phone, showing history and advice for an exercise"
              widths={[160, 320]}
              sizes="(min-width: 40rem) 11rem, 30vw"
            />
            <figcaption>Progress and advice</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <Image
              src={aiImport} data-full={full.aiImport}
              alt="Tetsu’s import screen on a phone, where a pasted routine is reviewed before it is saved"
              widths={[160, 320]}
              sizes="(min-width: 40rem) 11rem, 30vw"
            />
            <figcaption>Import and review</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <Image class="logo" src={logo} alt="The Tetsu logo" widths={[400, 800]} sizes="(min-width: 64rem) 31rem, 92vw" />
        </div>
        <ul data-reveal>
          <li>
            The AI import tries a local parser first, caps usage, checks the AI’s output and always
            ends on a review screen.
          </li>
          <li>
            Backed by 75 automated tests, 61 browser test cases and a 13-case validation matrix of
            synthetic training histories that found three defects in the live app. All three are
            fixed and covered by tests.
          </li>
          <li>
            Usage analytics and a PostHog dashboard are set up. Real usage numbers aren’t in yet, so
            I’m not quoting any.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="actions" data-reveal style="margin-top:0">
          <a class="btn" href="/work/tetsu/">Read the case study</a>
          <a class="textlink" href="https://tetsugym.ai.studio" rel="noopener">Open the live app</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="piece compact">
        <h3 data-reveal>Inbound bottleneck analysis, Amazon</h3>
        <p class="meta" data-reveal>Area Manager Intern, summer 2025</p>
        <p data-reveal>
          Alarm and downtime data showed that one unreliable loop was behind most of an inbound scan
          system’s stops. I proposed rerouting to two steadier lines and removing a manual role,
          with a projected 10 to 15% throughput gain.
        </p>
        <a class="textlink" href="/work/amazon/" data-reveal>Read the breakdown</a>
      </article>

      <article class="piece compact">
        <h3 data-reveal>Student events app, CCNY Capstone Challenge</h3>
        <p class="meta" data-reveal>Team Lead, Braven Accelerator, fall 2023</p>
        <p data-reveal>
          Our team of eight researched why students skip campus events and prototyped a better
          student life app. I led the research and presented to academic leadership, and we won the
          challenge.
        </p>
        <a class="textlink" href="/work/capstone/" data-reveal>Read the project</a>
      </article>

      <article class="piece compact">
        <h3 data-reveal>DvzzPins, a pin brand</h3>
        <p class="meta" data-reveal>Founder, December 2020 to October 2022</p>
        <p data-reveal>
          I took pins from my own sketches to finished products with a designer and a manufacturer,
          then launched them as drops. The first drop took 40 orders in a single day.
        </p>
        <a class="textlink" href="/work/dvzzpins/" data-reveal>See how it came together</a>
      </article>
</div>
    </section>

    <section id="about" class="band">
<div class="col">
      <h2 data-reveal>about</h2>
      <p data-reveal>
        I finished my BA in Management and Administration at The City College of New York in
        September 2026, magna cum laude. I like building working software with AI assistants, and I
        treat it like any other delivery: write down what it should do, test it, and check the
        results. Outside work I lift, and I used to produce and sell beats online.
      </p>
      <figure class="about-photo" data-reveal>
        <Image
          src={hackathon}
          alt="David, wearing an FDM jacket and lanyard, with a colleague talking to a participant at the Computershare Copilot Hackathon"
          widths={[480, 800, 1100]}
          sizes="(min-width: 64rem) 34rem, 92vw"
        />
        <figcaption>Supporting Computershare’s Copilot Hackathon for FDM.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <dl class="facts" data-reveal>
        <div>
          <dt>Based in</dt>
          <dd>New York</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Languages</dt>
          <dd>English, Spanish (fluent)</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Education</dt>
          <dd>BA, The City College of New York, GPA 3.5</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <div class="exp">
      <h3 class="group" data-reveal>Experience</h3>
      <ul class="rows">
        <li data-reveal>
          <div class="head"><span>Change &amp; Transformation Consultant, FDM Group</span><span class="when">Aug 2026 to now</span></div>
          <p>
            An eight-week consulting readiness program covering business analysis, Agile/Scrum, SAFe and
            Power BI. I supported Computershare’s Copilot hackathon, troubleshooting Copilot Studio
            workflows and building Power Automate workflows for participants.</p>
        </li>
        <li data-reveal>
          <div class="head"><span>Warehouse Associate / IT Superuser, Amazon, Melville NY</span><span class="when">Oct 2024 to Aug 2026</span></div>
          <p>
            First-line IT support for thin clients, monitors and scanners: diagnosing incidents, raising
            tickets and running daily equipment-readiness audits.</p>
        </li>
        <li data-reveal>
          <div class="head"><span>Area Manager Intern, Amazon, Hazleton PA</span><span class="when">Jun to Aug 2025</span></div>
          <p>The inbound bottleneck analysis above.</p>
        </li>
        <li data-reveal>
          <div class="head"><span>Team Lead, Braven Accelerator</span><span class="when">Aug to Dec 2023</span></div>
          <p>
            Coordinated timelines, research and the final presentation for a university app redesign.
            The team won the Fall 2023 Capstone Challenge.</p>
        </li>
        <li data-reveal>
          <div class="head"><span>Founder, DvzzPins</span><span class="when">Dec 2020 to Oct 2022</span></div>
          <p>The pin brand above.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="skills-block">
      <h3 class="group" data-reveal>Skills and tools</h3>
      <ul class="rows">
        <li data-reveal>
          <div class="head"><span>Analysis</span></div>
          <p>
            Requirements elicitation, user stories, acceptance criteria, process mapping,
            stakeholder analysis, root-cause analysis, RAID documentation, process improvement,
            incident triage, SQL for reporting and investigation
          </p>
        </li>
        <li data-reveal>
          <div class="head"><span>Delivery</span></div>
          <p>Agile/Scrum, SAFe</p>
        </li>
        <li data-reveal>
          <div class="head"><span>AI workflows</span></div>
          <p>Human-in-the-loop AI, document-grounded agents, prototyping with AI coding assistants</p>
        </li>
        <li data-reveal>
          <div class="head"><span>Tools</span></div>
          <p>Excel, Power BI, Microsoft 365, Copilot Studio, Power Automate, Shopify</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
      </div>
</div>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
<div class="col">
      <h2 data-reveal>contact</h2>
      <p class="statement" data-reveal>
        I’m looking for business analysis, implementation and workflow automation roles, including AI
        workflow work. If you have a messy problem, I’d like to hear about it.
      </p>
      <div class="contact" data-reveal>
        <Image
          src={headshot}
          alt="David Salazar"
          width={288}
          height={288}
          densities={[1, 2]}
        />
        <div>
          <p style="margin:0">
            <a class="big" href="mailto:davesal0710@gmail.com">davesal0710@gmail.com</a>
            <a class="big" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/davidsval">linkedin.com/in/davidsval</a>
            <a class="big" href="/David_Salazar_Resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Resume (PDF)</a>
          </p>
          <p class="muted small" style="margin-top:0.75rem">New York</p>
        </div>
      </div>
</div>
    </section>
  

  <script>
    const heroClip = document.querySelector<HTMLImageElement>('.hero-phone img[data-poster]');
    if (heroClip && matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) heroClip.src = heroClip.dataset.poster ?? heroClip.src;
    const demo = document.querySelector('[data-demo]');
    if (demo) {
      const panes = [...demo.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-pane]')];
      const seg = document.createElement('div');
      seg.className = 'seg';
      seg.setAttribute('role', 'group');
      seg.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Steps from a note to a requirement');
      const show = (i: number) => {
        panes.forEach((p, j) => {
          p.classList.toggle('is-active', j === i);
          p.inert = j !== i;
        });
        [...seg.children].forEach((b, j) => b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(j === i)));
      };
      panes.forEach((p, i) => {
        const b = document.createElement('button');
        b.type = 'button';
        b.textContent = p.dataset.label ?? '';
        b.addEventListener('click', () => show(i));
        seg.append(b);
      });
      demo.before(seg);
      show(0);
    }
  </script>
</Base>
